@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-experiments-explicit-local-consent
Every experimental feature MUST default off, persist separately from ordinary choices,
and remain device-local: account sync, old review data and existing accessibility
permission MUST NOT enable it. Changes MUST use the host's existing opt-out-aware
analytics boundary. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 experimental/opt-in/removability request,
including the browser floaty follow-up.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-settings-keep-existing-preferences
Shared AppSettings MUST remain Compose-reactive and retain the existing `pulls-ui`
keys, defaults and value encodings. Android MUST keep using its existing preference
file; iOS MUST store the same nonsecret choices through native storage. Storage and
effects MUST NOT introduce a shared-domain or shared-client dependency on Compose.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 same-app iOS decision and the accepted shared-presentation
AppSettings boundary in the iOS implementation plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-settings-sync-preserves-local-edits
A local synced preference edit MUST persist its value and notify the host's touched
callback, which retains ownership of change timestamps and synchronization. Applying
a synced value MUST update the reactive state and storage without touching its local
timestamp or reporting a new local change. Unknown names and unsupported values MUST
return false without changing the stored choice. Source: `data-settings-sync`, Tavi,
16 Oct 12:47; retained by the 21 Oct 2026 iOS reuse decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-settings-usage-opt-out-is-local
Usage stats and update notifications MUST remain local-only and MUST NOT appear in
syncedValue. Disabling usage stats MUST call the host's opt-out effect immediately
and MUST NOT report the disabling action as an analytics event. Enabling it MAY report
the first new usage-stats event after the host enables its queue. Source: root
`analytics-can-be-turned-off`, `data-settings-sync`, Tavi's 15 Oct 21:12 analytics
decision and 21 Oct 2026 iOS reuse decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-settings-zoom-preview-does-not-persist
A code-zoom preview MUST update the reactive value within the existing zoom limits
without persisting it or touching its sync timestamp. Committing the zoom MUST save
the clamped value and notify the touched callback. Source: recording 16 Oct 09:50,
04:11 to 04:26 (M9), retained by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 shared-settings decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-settings-sync-belongs-to-the-opening-source
Settings synchronization MUST retain the existing per-setting timestamp merge,
oldest-time adoption, local-edit reread and 1500ms debounce. A delayed call or debounce
for an old account/server/Access source MUST NOT send to or apply values to its
replacement. Unsupported remote settings MUST retain their existing local values.
Usage stats, update notifications and credential configuration MUST remain local.
Source: existing data-settings-sync, Tavi 16 Oct 12:47 and the 21 Oct 2026 source
ownership plan for the full shared iOS app.
